{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug — FINAL REPORT\n\n**Gerrit change:** [2449](https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2449) — commit `907b3f547994`, Change-Id `Id95805a840202c935916804af9c9a852b0f01811`. Pushed to `refs/for/main`; awaiting `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1`. Ticket stays **in_progress** — close is deferred until the change lands (Verified +1), per the Gerrit policy.\n\n### Root cause (proven)\n`config.py::reconciler_repo_root()` resolved the reconciler default root as `Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]` — the **package location**. Editable install: package lives in the checkout → correct. Non-editable/wheel install: package lives in `site-packages` → `parents[2]` = `<venv>/lib/pythonX`, not a checkout. Confirmed at runtime by simulating a site-packages `__file__`, reproducing the exact CI string `Resolved repo_root PosixPath('.../.venv/lib/python3.13')`. Production sets `REBAR_ROOT` so it never bites; the sweep legs that unset it expose it.\n\n### Discriminating proof\nAt the owned seam, `REBAR_ROOT` unset + non-editable-shaped `__file__` + non-checkout CWD: **before** → returns the venv path silently; **after** → raises the clear step-4 error. Same inputs but CWD inside a checkout: **after** → returns that checkout (step 3). Controls (`REBAR_ROOT` set; editable install) unchanged.\n\n### Defect origin (caused_by)\n`git blame`/`-S`/`--follow` traced the package-location-as-default: born in bootstrap `b534f47a` (3rd commit, **untrailered** — pre-convention carrier), deliberately re-established in `config.py` by C3a-CORE `d361eb28` (ticket **ba8b-c728-8c62-48e9**). Attributed `caused_by=ba8b`, class **plan_defect** (owned-default design that assumed editable install; a reviewer could have caught the non-editable case). Link recorded on this ticket.\n\n### Fix (Option C — validated layered fallback)\n`reconciler_repo_root()` now resolves: 1) `REBAR_ROOT` verbatim; 2) else package root **IF `_is_repo_checkout`**; 3) else `_git_toplevel_of_cwd()` **IF `_is_repo_checkout`**; 4) else a clear `RuntimeError` naming BOTH `REBAR_ROOT` and `--repo-root`. Package root is tried before CWD → daemon-from-anywhere / CWD-independence preserved; CWD is fallback-only and only when itself a checkout. Helpers: `_is_repo_checkout(root)` = `(.git exists) and (src/rebar is_dir)`; `_git_toplevel_of_cwd()` runs a **bounded** (`timeout=10`) `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, `check=False`, degrading to `None` on `OSError`/`SubprocessError` (git-absent, non-zero exit, timeout) so failures fall through to step 4 rather than an opaque traceback.\n\n### RED→GREEN (RED-first, held out, mutation-checked)\nRED tests appended to `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_core_seam_clean_heldout.py`, proven RED for the right reason BEFORE the fix, then held out from the fixer (a subagent got the contract only). After restore: GREEN. **Mutation check** (macOS `sandbox-exec`): reverting the exact defect returned the tests to RED (teeth). Legs: raise-on-non-checkout (discriminating), validated CWD fallback, `REBAR_ROOT`-verbatim + editable-install controls, and a **git-probe-failure** leg (stub `FileNotFoundError`/`TimeoutExpired` → still the clear step-4 error; independently mutation-verified — narrowing the catch to `OSError`-only turns the timeout leg RED). No test weakening — only additive.\n\n### Step-7 sibling sweep\nConstruct swept: `Path(__file__).resolve().parents[N]` package-location-as-repo-root.\n- **CONFIRMED siblings — `fetcher.py:507` & `:626`** (`Path(repo_root_env() or Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4])`): same class (non-checkout venv path under non-editable when `REBAR_ROOT` unset), bypassing the owned resolver. **Fixed in scope** — both now call `config.reconciler_repo_root()`, closing the construct sibling AND the parity gap (every reconciler surface now resolves repo-root through the single validated resolver). Guarded by a **construct-uniqueness test** (RED with the two fetcher sites present, GREEN after).\n- **NOT a sibling — `__main__.py:52`** (`_pkg_parent = ...parents[3]`): resolves the package *parent* for a `sys.path` import bootstrap; correct under both install modes. Excluded.\n\n### Scope / safety\nCaller sweep: `invariants._default_repo_root` and ~11 reconciler sites already route through the owned resolver (unchanged); fetcher was the lone bypass (now fixed). Restoration-not-creation: preserves the two working cases (`REBAR_ROOT` set; editable install). No new deps (`subprocess` is stdlib). Gates green: `make lint` (ruff + format + complexity ratchet + module-size — config.py under the 800-LOC cap, functions under the mccabe ceiling via the two extracted helpers) and `make typecheck` (715 files, clean). Regression sweep: seam suite + `test_reconcile_main.py` + `fetch/` = 64 passed. `docs/env-vars.md` regenerated (generated artifact; line-number churn only).\n\n### Replication\nThe original `test_reconcile_main.py` resolution legs pass; the non-editable scenario now resolves to the real checkout via the CWD fallback (was `<venv>/lib/python3.13`).\n\n### Plan-review gate\n`review_plan` re-run after declaring the sibling scope (file_impact += fetcher.py + the guard test) → **PASS**, attested/signed, no blocking findings. Advisories (all non-blocking) concerned `_git_toplevel_of_cwd()` subprocess-failure robustness — addressed proactively (bounded timeout + `SubprocessError` catch + the git-probe-failure test), and one AC-wording note (compound \"and\" criteria).\n\n### Residual risk\n- Step 3 depends on `git` on PATH; a git-absent/hung environment degrades cleanly to the step-4 error (tested), not a silent wrong root.\n- A directory that is a git repo but not a rebar checkout is rejected by `_is_repo_checkout` (requires `src/rebar`), so a non-rebar CWD cannot mis-resolve.\n- `REBAR_ROOT` remains authoritative and unvalidated by design (operator's explicit choice) — unchanged.\n\n**Close disposition:** deferred to post-merge. When change 2449 reaches `Verified +1` (+ `LLM-Review +1`) and lands, close with `--class=plan_defect --caused-by=ba8b-c728-8c62-48e9`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788133319925248359,"uuid":"e550c078-cef0-4701-86ea-6efd5a67438d"}